<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Æthelwold ætheling</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 902</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Æthelwold was a West <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> prince, the son of King Æthelred I and cousin of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-the-elder">Edward the Elder</a>. On the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfred-the-great">Alfred the Great</a> in 899 he seized Wimborne and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christchurch">Christchurch</a> to claim the throne, then fled to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danes">Danes</a> of Northumbria, who accepted him as king. He was killed in 902 at the Battle of the Holme, fighting with the East Anglian Danes against Edward.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aethelwold-aetheling.jpg" alt="Æthelwold ætheling" width="320" height="399" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hel-hama · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:England_878.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
